= Solution
{parent=c}

Here the vertical bars denote <determinants>. Since $B=B^{-1}$, taking <determinants> gives $(\det B)^2=1$. The condition $\det B>0$ selects $\det B=1$. By the multiplicative property of the <determinant>,
$$
\boxed{\det A=\frac{\det(AB)}{\det B}=\frac{-2}{1}=-2.}
$$
The hypotheses determine this <determinant>, while allowing many possible <matrices> $A$ and $B$.

